# Optional host port for the standalone release compose.yaml. No .env is required.
# The downloaded Compose file works without this template or a source checkout.
# PORT=3000
# Data is mounted from ./data beside compose.yaml to /data in the container.
# Linux, before the first start: sudo install -d -o 1000 -g 1000 -m 0700 ./data
# Windows Docker Desktop: create data and allow Docker access using host ACLs.
# Complete first-time administrator setup through localhost or an SSH tunnel
# before exposing a public reverse proxy. The master key is generated automatically.
# Existing volume deployments must stop, back up and restore all data before switching.
# PORT configures the host mapping; it is not injected into the container.
# Directory preparation, migration and advanced overrides:
# https://github.com/ZeonXr/oci-dash/blob/main/docs/OPERATIONS.md
